Now if you step back and look at the entire architecture you’ve explained so far, you have three major operational departments:

Policyholder Lane
     ↓
Collect Claim
Claim Adjuster Lane
     ↓
Investigate & Assess Claim
SIU Lane
     ↓
Investigate Fraud
Vendor Manager Lane
     ↓
Inspect, Repair & Manage Vendors

And all four of these are coordinated by the Claims Orchestration / Brain Agent sitting in the middle of the diagram. That Brain Agent is the equivalent of your “Mera Brain” in the underwriting project. It decides which agent should run next, shares context between agents, and manages the entire end-to-end claims workflow.
